{"Removing the coarse cacheMu lock from bleveBackend.BuildIndex allows multiple goroutines to build the same index concurrently because getOrCreateIndex has no per-key coordination, which can cause concurrent creation of the same directory/index and nondeterministic failures or corruption for file-backed indices": 0.8359171748161316, "bleveBackend.TotalDocs iterates b.cache without any lock while BuildIndex writes to the same map, which can crash the process with a fatal 'concurrent map iteration and map write' during Prometheus collection": 0.5644469261169434, "Watch channel close panic: Init now always runs during NewResourceServer, the watcher goroutine reads from events channel without checking ok and then dereferences v, which can panic when the backend closes the events channel during Stop": 0.40129178762435913, "searchSupport.init has Go concurrency bugs: the loop variable info is captured by goroutines and totalBatchesIndexed++ is unsynchronized, causing incorrect indexing/metrics and data races": 0.4663403034210205, "The integration test is now skipped for Postgres, reducing CI coverage for a supported DB and risking regressions going unnoticed": 0.8178910613059998}